<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/93675b06cdb1> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[204] LOS ANGELES During this week’s wildfires, navigation apps like Waze and Google Maps were guiding drivers into evacuation areas" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "204" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c26a0637a266> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[207] LOS ANGELES During this week’s wildfires, navigation apps like Waze and Google Maps were guiding drivers into evacuation areas and caused congestion where officials were ordering streets closed, according to a motion introduced by Los Angeles City Councilman Paul Koretz on Friday, Dec. 8." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "207" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cf3d05b28d06> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Los Angeles Police Department cautioned drivers this week not to use navigation apps like Google Maps and Waze while trying to find their way from a fire zone." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "205" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f7b86c3f4de9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[203] Mobile traffic applications such as Waze are causing a dangerous flood of traffic to be funneled onto tiny Los Angeles side streets." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "203" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a1e3e6d6c692> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The issue wasn’t specific to Waze either, drivers using Apple Maps and Google Maps were having similar issues." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "199" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/034f1489c5eb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The motion would also ask the department what efforts it has made to get the app companies to address neighborhood concerns, call on the city attorney to analyze whether app companies share liability for damages in collisions caused by their users, and urge the City Council to request the app companies make their representatives available to work with the city." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "203" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/156ed725cecd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The company tweeted on Thursday that it was working with the Los Angeles Department of Transportation and other Waze users to mark road closures and shelters along routes." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "199" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1906621f7203> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"We worked really hard Wednesday afternoon to get our maps up to date and accurate,\" Waze spokeswoman Chelsea Russo told USA Today." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "197" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3bab72ff79b5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Los Angeles Police Department was alerting users of navigation apps to avoid using them so they don't end up near the blazes." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "196" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5f6498d68915> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "On assignment to cover the fires, a USA TODAY reporter midmorning Wednesday looked to Waze for an alternative route to the Getty Center museum." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "200" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8cf95897047a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Waze says that it’s been working to correct the issue." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "198" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/98df1a612c47> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Waze's Russo said the LAPD was working off Wednesday morning information." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "206" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9964676eaf86> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Waze, which also works with transportation authorities and a team of local map editors to keep the app updated, says on any given day, those enflamed neighborhoods would have been shown as off limits within an hour of two." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "206" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a703cb95a0b8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Los Angeles Police Department was alerting users of navigation apps to avoid using them so they don't end up near the blazes, reported The Los Angeles Times." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "206" .

